    "body": "> Hi, [@janewman](https://github.com/janewman)\n> \n> I had worked on the Spatial Navigation (https://www.w3.org/TR/css-nav-1/), which defines a general model for navigating the focus using the arrow keys, as well as related CSS, JavaScript features and Events.\n> \n> I also deep dived into the aria concerns and how to move focus in the scrollable area. Do you think there is any cross-passing between the Spatial Navigation and the `focusgroup` attributes?\n\nHi @jihyerish, these two features both have a goal of making it easier to use the web without a mouse, and in my opinion, should work well together.\n\nWhile these two APIs have different goals (moving focus within a composite widget vs navigating the page), I think there are a few shared concepts that might be worth looking into such as triggering and key-conflicts (content that also uses the same inputs as focusgroup/spacial navigation). I'd be curious to hear your thoughts, feel free to bring them up here or in https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
