    "body": "Regarding what I mentioned in the meeting. Current behaviour of focusgroup and popover is a bit of an odd one. Given the below markup, you can arrow between the buttons and but if activate the popover from Item 2, you'll see its internal button is at the end of the focusgroup when arrowing. This feels wrong to me, it should probably be excluded from the focusgroup by default. Perhaps the top layer should be an exclusion criteria?\n\n```html\n<div focusgroup=\"toolbar\">\n  <button>Item 1</button>\n  <button popovertarget=\"foobar\">\n    Item 2\n  </button>\n  <button>Item 3</button>\n  <div popover id=\"foobar\">\n    <button>Popover Item</button>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<style>\n  [popover] {\n    inset: auto;\n    top: anchor(bottom);\n    left: anchor(right);\n  }\n</style>\n```\n\nhttps://codepen.io/lukewarlow/pen/KwgjvpZ - Here's another case that's even weirder, where you can't access the popover children by simply tabbing anymore.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
